<auto_mode_integration>

## How Auto-Mode Reads UI Consistency Context

Auto-mode does NOT automatically scan `.gsd/ui-gates/`. The LLM must explicitly read artifacts during discuss phase.

### Required Actions in Discuss Phase

1. **Check if design system exists:**
   ```bash
   ls .gsd/ui-gates/STYLE_PICK.md .gsd/ui-gates/DESIGN_DNA.md .gsd/ui-gates/COMPONENT_PLAN.md 2>/dev/null
   ```

2. **Read design system:**
   ```
   Read .gsd/ui-gates/STYLE_PICK.md
   Read .gsd/ui-gates/DESIGN_DNA.md
   Read .gsd/ui-gates/COMPONENT_PLAN.md
   ```

3. **Read audit (if exists):**
   ```
   Read .gsd/ui-gates/AUDIT.md
   Read .gsd/ui-gates/PRIORITY.md
   ```

4. **Use in milestone planning:**
   - Apply STYLE_PICK colors/spacing to new components
   - Follow COMPONENT_PLAN state/sizes for component design
   - Respect DESIGN_DNA anti-patterns
   - Prioritize fixes from AUDIT.md in slice planning

### Memory Injection

`loadMemoryBlock()` automatically injects memories from `capture_thought()` into every auto-mode prompt. Capture these during ui-consistency:
- Token patterns (color scales, spacing scales)
- Component boundaries (what belongs in design system vs app)
- Accessibility requirements
- Performance constraints

</auto_mode_integration>

